Appendix 1: Graph Counts
Tables 12–15 below contain all known exact counts of (3, k; n, e)-graphs for speciﬁed n,
for k = 7, 8, 9 and 10, respectively. All graph counts were obtained by the algorithms
described in Section 3. Empty entries indicate 0. In all cases, the maximum number
of edges is bounded by ∆(G)n/2 ≤ (k − 1)n/2. All (3, ≤ 9; n, ≤ e(3, k, n) + 1)-graphs
which were constructed by our programs can be obtained from the House of Graphs [3]
by searching for the keywords “minimal ramsey graph” or from [7].


