codex
The bounded packing LP passes a deliberately constructed \(H\), so the sample result does not give a universal exclusion. That \(H\) has ten independent eight-sets that meet every other independent eight-set. I will now add the next constraint: an independent seven-set can avoid at most two selected neighbourhoods. This gives a precise LP test without an SDP solver.
